From: seilent <github@seilent.net>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 16:30:59 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: q6afe: wait for the ADSP before adding the clock
 controller

q6afe_probe() adds its child devices, the clock controller among them,
as soon as the AFE service is registered. After an ADSP restart the
clock consumers probe again within a few milliseconds and send their
LPASS core votes, and some of those votes fail.

The probe now defers until q6core reports the ADSP ready, as q6prm does.
When q6core is not bound yet the check fails and the probe is retried
once q6core binds.
---
 sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe.c b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe.c
index 22ccee25c..d7e5e4c70 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe.c
@@ -1924,6 +1924,9 @@ static int q6afe_probe(struct apr_device *adev)
 	struct q6afe *afe;
 	struct device *dev = &adev->dev;
 
+	if (!q6core_is_adsp_ready())
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, -EPROBE_DEFER, "ADSP not ready\n");
+
 	afe = devm_kzalloc(dev, sizeof(*afe), GFP_KERNEL);
 	if (!afe)
 		return -ENOMEM;
